 "Azure Cosmos DB":{summary:"A globally distributed NoSQL database for low-latency JSON, key-value, graph and wide-column workloads.",focus:"partition keys, logical partitions, consistency and request units",flow:"API request routes to a partition, executes against an item and returns a consistency-controlled result",fit:"Use it for globally distributed operational data with predictable low-latency access patterns.",boundary:"account, database, container and partition-key boundary",watch:"a poor partition key creates hot partitions and throttling that scaling the account alone will not fix",alternative:"Azure SQL Database for relational transactions and T-SQL joins",cost:"provisioned or serverless throughput, storage, regions, backup, networking and analytical features",hook:"Cosmos DB decisions start with partition key and consistency; it is not a relational SQL replacement."},
 "Azure Database for PostgreSQL":{summary:"A managed PostgreSQL database service for running relational workloads with Azure operations, backups, scaling and connectivity.",focus:"PostgreSQL engine compatibility, compute tier, storage and extensions",flow:"application connects through a private or controlled endpoint, executes a transaction and commits to managed storage",fit:"Use it for PostgreSQL applications that need managed backups, patching and high availability.",boundary:"server, database, role and network boundary",watch:"extension support, connection limits and long-running transactions can constrain lift-and-shift designs",alternative:"Azure Database for PostgreSQL Flexible Server for the current deployment model and controls",cost:"compute, provisioned storage, IOPS, backups, networking and replicas",hook:"PostgreSQL compatibility plus managed relational operations points to Azure Database for PostgreSQL."},
