 "Azure SQL Managed Instance":{summary:"A managed SQL Server instance with broad engine compatibility and instance-scoped features while Azure operates the underlying platform.",focus:"instance boundary, SQL Agent, native backup and VNet integration",flow:"application connects to the instance, executes compatible SQL Server workloads and persists to managed HA storage",fit:"Use it for SQL Server migrations needing instance-level capabilities with less infrastructure administration.",boundary:"managed instance, subnet, database and T-SQL compatibility boundary",watch:"subnet sizing, maintenance behavior and feature compatibility still require migration assessment",alternative:"Azure SQL Database for cloud-native database-level simplicity",cost:"vCore compute, storage, backup, licensing model, networking and replicas",hook:"Managed Instance is chosen for SQL Server compatibility at the instance boundary, not merely for database hosting."},
 "Azure Cache for Redis":{summary:"A managed in-memory Redis-compatible cache for low-latency reads, sessions, queues and transient application state.",focus:"keys, TTLs, eviction, persistence and clustered capacity",flow:"application checks cache first, falls back to the source of truth and refreshes entries with explicit invalidation",fit:"Use it to reduce read latency and database load for cacheable data or coordinated transient state.",boundary:"cache instance, database/keyspace and network boundary",watch:"cache contents are not automatically the source of truth and eviction or failover can expose stale/missing data",alternative:"Azure Managed Redis for the newer managed Redis offering",cost:"cache tier, nodes, capacity, persistence, replicas and network transfer",hook:"Redis accelerates access; design cache-aside, TTL and invalidation rather than treating it as the system of record."},
 "Azure Managed Redis":{summary:"A managed Redis service for high-performance caching, session state, messaging and data structures with Azure-managed operations.",focus:"Redis data structures, availability, persistence and access policy",flow:"application uses a managed Redis endpoint for hot data while durable records remain in a primary database",fit:"Use it when Redis-compatible performance and managed availability are required for latency-sensitive paths.",boundary:"managed Redis resource, database/keyspace and client identity boundary",watch:"key expiration, memory pressure and failover behavior must be tested against application retry logic",alternative:"Azure Cache for Redis when an existing cache deployment and feature set is the better fit",cost:"capacity, replicas, persistence, storage, networking and client operations",hook:"Managed Redis is a hot-data acceleration layer; durable business truth belongs in a durable store."},
 "Azure Database for MariaDB":{summary:"A managed MariaDB relational database service for compatible application workloads with Azure-operated backups and maintenance.",focus:"MariaDB compatibility, server configuration, storage and connectivity",flow:"application connects to the managed server, executes relational transactions and relies on automated backup/maintenance controls",fit:"Use it for existing MariaDB applications while planning the supported migration or modernization path.",boundary:"server, database, account and network boundary",watch:"engine/version support and migration lifecycle matter because MariaDB service availability and options can change",alternative:"Azure Database for MySQL when application compatibility permits a current MySQL target",cost:"compute, storage, backups, networking and migration/replication overhead",hook:"Validate the MariaDB service lifecycle and engine compatibility before committing a new design."},
 "Azure Database Migration Service":{summary:"A managed migration service for moving database schemas and data between supported source and target engines with controlled cutover workflows.",focus:"online/offline migration, schema conversion, validation and cutover",flow:"source is assessed and replicated, target is validated, then application connections are switched during cutover",fit:"Use it for repeatable database migration with reduced downtime where source and target are supported.",boundary:"migration project, source/target credentials and replication boundary",watch:"schema incompatibilities, long-running transactions and unreplicated side effects can invalidate a cutover plan",alternative:"Data Factory for general data movement and transformation rather than database migration semantics",cost:"migration compute, replication duration, networking, validation and target resources",hook:"Database Migration Service moves databases and manages migration workflow; it does not redesign application schemas automatically."},
 "Azure Database for PostgreSQL Flexible Server":{summary:"A current managed PostgreSQL deployment model with configurable compute, maintenance windows, networking, backups and high availability.",focus:"flexible-server compute, zone-redundant HA, private access and maintenance",flow:"application uses a private PostgreSQL endpoint while the service manages backups, patching and optional standby failover",fit:"Use it for new PostgreSQL workloads and migrations needing more control than a legacy single-server model.",boundary:"flexible server, delegated subnet, database and HA boundary",watch:"HA protects service availability but does not replace transaction retry or application-level recovery testing",alternative:"Azure Database for PostgreSQL when compatibility with an existing deployment is the constraint",cost:"compute, storage, IOPS, backup retention, HA standby and network transfer",hook:"Flexible Server adds current deployment controls; HA standby is not a read-scaling substitute by default."},
 "Azure Database for MySQL Flexible Server":{summary:"A managed MySQL deployment model with configurable compute, private networking, maintenance windows, backups and availability options.",focus:"flexible-server sizing, private access, HA and maintenance control",flow:"application connects privately to MySQL, commits transactions and uses managed backup or standby recovery paths",fit:"Use it for new MySQL workloads and migrations needing controlled maintenance and networking.",boundary:"flexible server, delegated subnet, database and HA boundary",watch:"connection pooling, storage growth and failover retry behavior should be tested before production",alternative:"Azure Database for MySQL when an existing service shape must be preserved",cost:"compute, storage, IOPS, backup, HA and network transfer",hook:"Flexible Server is the current MySQL managed deployment choice when private networking and lifecycle control matter."},
